1
00:00:01,253 --> 00:00:08,593
(Q11（配对题）) Good morning, and welcome to the museum - one with a remarkable range of exhibits, which I'm sure you'll enjoy.

2
00:00:08,593 --> 00:00:13,202
My name's Greg, and I'll tell you about the various collections as we go round.

3
00:00:13,202 --> 00:00:17,408
But before we go, let me just give you a taste of what we have here.

4
00:00:17,408 --> 00:00:24,620
[Q11可能是干扰项(D)， 提到artist，但并不是D be given by artists] Well, for one thing, we have a fine collection of twentieth and twenty-first century paintings, many by very well-known artists.

5
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:27,321
I'm sure you'll recognise several of the paintings.

6
00:00:27,321 --> 00:00:34,463
[Q11答案句（E）attract largest number =  most popular] This is the gallery that attracts the largest number of visitors, so it's best to go in early in the day, before the crowds arrive.

7
00:00:34,463 --> 00:00:37,576
(Q12) Then there are the nineteenth-century paintings.

8
00:00:37,576 --> 00:00:45,829
[Q12答案句（D） donate=given] The museum was opened in the middle of that century, and several of the artists each donated one work - to get the museum started, as it were.

9
00:00:45,829 --> 00:00:50,853
So they're of special interest to us - we feel closer to them than to other works.

10
00:00:50,853 --> 00:00:57,240
(Q13) The sculpture gallery has a number of fine exhibits, but I'm afraid it's currently closed for refurbishment.

11
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:04,141
[Q13答案句（G） move = relocate] You'll need to come back next year to see it properly, but a number of the sculptures have been moved to other parts of the museum.

12
00:01:04,141 --> 00:01:11,742
(Q14) [Q14答案句（B） TV or newspaper = media] 'Around the world' is a temporary exhibition - you've probably seen something about it on TV or in the newspapers.&nbsp;

13
00:01:11,742 --> 00:01:18,224
It's created a great deal of interest, because it presents objects from every continent and many countries,

14
00:01:18,224 --> 00:01:25,067
and provides information about their social context - why they were made, who for, and so on.

15
00:01:25,067 --> 00:01:27,393
(Q15) Then there's the collection of coins.

16
00:01:27,393 --> 00:01:38,034
This is what you might call a focused, specialist collection, because all the coins come from this country, and were produced between two thousand and a thousand years ago.

17
00:01:38,034 --> 00:01:44,575
[Q15答案句（C） ordinary people = members of the public] And many of them were discovered by ordinary people digging their gardens, and donated to the museum!

18
00:01:44,575 --> 00:01:50,587
(Q16) [Q16答案句（A）all was left to ... by ... =  one person] All our porcelain and glass was left to the museum by its founder, when he died in 1878.

19
00:01:50,587 --> 00:02:01,935
And in the terms of his will, we're not allowed to add anything to that collection: he believed it was perfect in itself, and we don't see any reason to disagree!

20
00:02:01,935 --> 00:02:09,431
(Q17（地图）) OK, that was something about the collections, and now here's some more practical information, in case you need it.

21
00:02:09,431 --> 00:02:16,383
Most of the museum facilities are downstairs, in the basement, so you go down the stairs here.

22
00:02:16,383 --> 00:02:20,461
When you reach the bottom of the stairs, you'll find yourself in a sitting area,

23
00:02:20,461 --> 00:02:27,419
with comfortable chairs and sofas where you can have a rest before continuing your exploration of the museum.

24
00:02:27,419 --> 00:02:33,600
We have a very good restaurant, which serves excellent food all day, in a relaxing atmosphere.

25
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:43,492
[Q17答案句(找restaurant)] To reach it, when you get to the bottom of the stairs, go straight ahead to the far side of the sitting area, then turn right into the corridor.

26
00:02:43,492 --> 00:02:47,216
You'll see the door of the restaurant facing you.

27
00:02:47,216 --> 00:02:53,925
(Q18) If you just want a snack, or if you'd like to eat somewhere with facilities for children, we also have a cafe.

28
00:02:53,925 --> 00:03:04,478
[Q18答案句(找cafe)] When you reach the bottom of the stairs, you'll need to go straight ahead, turn right into the corridor, and the cafe is immediately on the right.

29
00:03:04,478 --> 00:03:09,360
(Q19) And talking about children, there are baby-changing facilities downstairs:

30
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:19,575
[Q19答案句(找baby-changing facilities)] Cross the sitting area, continue straight ahead along the corridor on the left, and you and your baby will find the facilities on the left-hand side.

31
00:03:19,575 --> 00:03:24,791
(Q20) The cloakroom, where you should leave coats, umbrellas and any large bags,&nbsp;

32
00:03:24,791 --> 00:03:32,508
[Q20答案句(找cloakroom)] is on the left hand side of the sitting area.&nbsp; &nbsp;It's through the last door before you come to the corridor.

33
00:03:32,508 --> 00:03:39,961
There are toilets on every floor, but in the basement they're the first rooms on the left when you get down there.

34
00:03:39,961 --> 00:03:42,461
OK, now if you've got anything to leave in the cloakroom, please do that now, and then we'll start our tour.

